  "prompt": "The game Miray asked for: you travel the world, visiting one country on each continent, and each country's level is themed to that continent. Brazil might have sugar plantations; in Africa you go to Egypt and there are the pyramids. Each country level has puzzles to solve, or quizzes and questions, tied to that place.\n\nTo travel from continent to continent you have to cross an ocean. That is its own level: you are swimming underwater, you get bigger by eating fish, you avoid sharks and bigger fish, and once you are big enough you reach the surface, find a boat, and hitch a ride to the next continent. The ocean level plays every time you cross between continents, but it is a different version each time so it is not boring or repetitive: the first crossing you are plankton, the next crossing you are a minnow or tiny fish, then tuna, then a shark, then a whale or an orca, something like that, each one a bigger creature with bigger threats.",
  "brief": "Un tour du monde : six pays, un par continent, chacun avec ses énigmes et son quiz — et cinq traversées d'océan où l'on grandit en mangeant, du plancton à l'orque, pour attraper le bateau vers la suite. / A world tour: six countries, one per continent, each with its own puzzle and quiz — and five ocean crossings where you grow by eating, from plankton to orca, to catch the boat onward.",
  "objective": "Stamp all six passports — solve each country's puzzle and quiz — then grow through five ocean crossings (plankton → minnow → tuna → shark → orca) and catch the boat that carries you around the world.",
